    "summary": "Strong Black Peter and Lovelight; guest vocalist drags finish",
    "blurb": "The early set shines with a heartfelt Black Peter and a blazing Turn On Your Lovelight. Hard To Handle adds fire, but the surprise guest’s appearance on the closing songs dulls the momentum. The Miller soundboard capture is excellent and showcases the band at its tightest.",
    "review": "On March 8, 1970 at Phoenix’s Travelodge Theatre in the Round, the Dead delivered a solid first set anchored by Jerry’s “sweet, musical and heartbreakingly passionate” vocals on Black Peter and an electrifying Turn On Your Lovelight. Hard To Handle rips through with raw energy, while the acoustic interludes keep the flow intimate. Unfortunately, an unannounced guest vocalist hijacks Not Fade Away, Impromptu Blues and the closing Lovelight, turning what could have been a soaring finish into a muddied ending. The Miller soundboard recording (gd1970-03-08.sbd.miller.113359.flac16) captures the band’s tight rhythm section and clear vocal blend with excellent clarity, making it the best source to experience this mixed‑quality performance.",
